Partial-knowledge evaluation
----------------------------

CAFA-evaluator-PK
    Clara De Paolis
    https://github.com/claradepaolis/CAFA-evaluator-PK

    Adds partial-knowledge evaluation (per-protein exclusion of annotations
    known at prediction time) and the terms-of-interest filter. This
    repository is a fork of that work.


Bootstrap resampling
--------------------

    Rashika Ramola introduced the bootstrap machinery in this line, including
    the replicate index handling (`B_ind`) and the per-replicate metric
    aggregation, in commits from 2025-02 onward.

    An Phan extended it to paired sampling across prediction files, so that a
    given replicate uses the same resampled targets for every method, and
    added `src/cafaeval/evaluation_bootstrap.py`.


Sparse evaluation
-----------------

cafaeval-protea
    Francisco Miguel Pérez Canales
    https://github.com/frapercan/cafaeval-protea

    Source of the sparse evaluation layer integrated here in August 2026:
    CSR storage for predictions, the sparse ontology DAG, the sparse NK/LK
    and PK confusion-matrix kernels, sparse and COO propagation, the
    PyArrow prediction parser, the `CAFAEVAL_SPARSE` and
    `CAFAEVAL_FAST_PARSER` environment gates, and the partial-knowledge
    coverage fix that restricts the coverage numerator to the
    post-exclusion population.


Parallel propagation
--------------------

CAFA-evaluator-PK-speedup
    Antonina Dolgorukova (GitHub: T0chka)
    https://github.com/T0chka/CAFA-evaluator-PK-speedup (branch speedup-local)

    Shared in the CAFA 6 Kaggle discussion "Speeding up cafaeval":
    https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/cafa-6-protein-function-prediction/discussion/664359

    The shared-memory parallel DAG propagation in graph.py, the cached
    per-term children map and the serial propagation helper originate in this
    work. They reached this repository through cafaeval-protea, which
    cherry-picked her commits with git authorship preserved.
